    "content": "The Speaker of the Puntland Parliament, Cabdirisaaq Axmed Siciid, opened a consultative meeting on Monday in Garowe between a special parliamentary committee and opposition politicians to deliberate on proposed amendments to the Puntland constitution, according to a report by Horseed Media. The meeting is part of efforts to build consensus on the constitutional review process.\n\nThe push to amend the constitution has been ongoing, with the Puntland government announcing plans to revise the charter. Opposition figures have raised concerns about the process, leading to the current consultative meeting aimed at bridging differences. The special committee, formed by the parliament, is tasked with gathering input from various stakeholders.\n\nThe opposition politicians present at the meeting included several prominent figures who have been critical of the government's approach. The discussions focused on the content of the proposed amendments and the need for broad-based consultation. The speaker emphasized the importance of inclusivity in the review process.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, particularly those with ties to Puntland, the outcome of the constitutional review is significant. Diaspora communities are actively engaged in Puntland's political and economic life, and changes to the constitution could affect their rights, investment opportunities, and political participation. Many diaspora members fund development projects and hold stakes in the region's stability.\n\nThis consultative meeting comes amid broader political dynamics in Puntland, including recent elections and ongoing debates over governance structures. The international community has urged Puntland's leaders to ensure that the constitutional review is transparent and participatory. The meeting is expected to produce recommendations that will inform the parliamentary debate on the amendments.\n\nThe speaker's initiative to engage the opposition directly is seen as a positive step toward reducing political tensions. However, it remains to be seen whether the opposition's concerns will be adequately addressed. The coming weeks will be crucial as the special committee finalizes its report and the parliament prepares for further deliberations.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/barlamaanka-puntland-siyaasiyiinta-mucaaradka-oo-ka-shiray-waxka-beddelka-dastuurka/427132/",
