    "summary": "The United Nations peacekeeping mission in Western Sahara is concluding after 35 years, following the Security Council's failure to extend its mandate, according to the UN Secretary-General.",
    "content": "The United Nations peacekeeping mission in Western Sahara, known as MINURSO, is set to end after 35 years of operation. The closure follows the Security Council's inability to renew the mission's mandate, as confirmed by the UN Secretary-General on Sunday. The decision marks the conclusion of one of the longest-running UN peacekeeping missions in Africa.\n\nMINURSO was established in 1991 to monitor a ceasefire between Morocco and the Polisario Front, which seeks independence for Western Sahara. The mission's mandate has been renewed annually, but this year, the Security Council failed to reach an agreement on its extension. The reasons for the failure were not immediately detailed, but the move signals a shift in the international approach to the long-standing dispute.\n\nThe conflict over Western Sahara dates back to 1975 when Spain withdrew from the territory. Morocco claims sovereignty, while the Polisario Front demands a referendum on self-determination. The UN has been involved in mediation efforts for decades, and MINURSO's presence has been seen as a stabilizing factor.\n\nThe end of the mission raises concerns about the potential for renewed hostilities and the impact on civilians in the region. It also underscores the challenges facing the Security Council in addressing protracted conflicts. For the Somali diaspora, the development is significant as it reflects the broader dynamics of international peacekeeping and the importance of sustained global engagement in conflict zones. Many Somalis have served in UN missions or have family members affected by similar operations, and the closure of MINURSO may prompt discussions on the effectiveness and future of UN peacekeeping.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/howlgalkii-nabad-ilaalinta-qaramada-midoobay-ee-galbeedka-saxaraha-oo-dhammaanaya-kaddib-35-sano/427127/",
